
    None of this will deal with non-ascii trivial chars
very well. If you need to deal with UTF-8 or similar then
you have a whole other stack of problems.

    Also the strtrim should not ever malloc or mess with memory
pointers that were passed to it. Bad undefined nose demon type
behavior will happen.

Regardless we don't seem to lose any memory anywhere : 

hydra$ uname -apKU
FreeBSD hydra 13.1-RELEASE-p3 FreeBSD 13.1-RELEASE-p3 GENERIC amd64 amd64 1301000 1301000

